#Introduction
Mobile technology has undergone a massive evolution from the days of Motorola and Nokia to present day iPhones. Mobile phones have moved from devices only capable of voice communication and SMS texting to all-in-one computers that have revolutionized the internet and made it an essential part of our lives. Mobile technology is getting more advanced as time goes on, with current flagships offering comparable computing power to desktops and laptops, keeping the same pocket-sized form factor.
In this case study, we aim to track the history of mobile technology and analyse its development along two viewpoints, from the first mobile phone to present day smartphones. We will analyze the impact that this evolution has had on both general society, such as access to the internet, online shopping and social networking. We will also analyse the impact it has had in the business world, such as improvements to communcation in and between companies, the rise of remote work and blurring of work-life boundaries. Finally, we will evaluate the ethical implications that the evolution of mobile technology has had so far and what it may lead to in the future.

